# Frontend environment (`fe/.env`)

Vite loads **`fe/.env`** at build/dev time (same committed file on Mac and Ubuntu). Client-visible keys reach `import.meta.env` only if they match an **`envPrefix`** in `fe/vite.config.mjs`: `VITE_`, `FE_`, `API_`, `VERTICAL_`, `HORIZONTAL_`, `DEBUG_`, `GLOBAL_`, `TOP_`, `RIGHT_`, `DIALOG_`, `FOOTER_`, `FOOTERPAGES_`, `MOBILE_`, `DESKTOP_`, `PRESS_`, `HOVER_`, `MY_PICKS_`, `VSINGLES_`, `RATE_`, `MAIN_`, `DEFAULT_`, `NEW_`, `THEME_`, `NOTIFICATION_`, `SPECIAL_`, `DISABLE_`, `PRICE_`, `SCAN_`, `RECORD_`, `SELF_`, `YELLOW_`, `NOTES_`, `PHOTOALBUMS_`, `ONENOTE_`, `ALBUM_`, `ALL_SINGLES_`, `PICKS_`, `ACQUAINTS_`, `ACQUAINT_`, `MYALBUM_`, `MYSELFREPORTBIO_`, `RECEIVED_`, `PROFILE_`, `TOPRIGHT_`, `SPEEDDATING`, `RAG_`, `LEFT_`, `SKIP_`, `BSIZE`. A new key without a matching prefix is **invisible** to the FE.

After changes: **restart Vite** on Mac (`feall`); on Ubuntu re-run the PM2 FE build (`work2` / `febeprod`). Backend-only keys live in **`~/.ssh/be/.env`** — see `be-env.mdc`.

## Keys mirrored from `~/.ssh/be/.env` (be.env wins)

`fe/vite.config.mjs` (`BE_ENV_KEYS_FROM_HOME_FILE`) reads these from `~/.ssh/be/.env` before bundling. **When set there, they override `fe/.env`** — so prod values come from Ubuntu `be.env` (`myscript/ubuntu/be.env`, refresh with `syncbenv`).

| Key | Prod `be.env` value | FE usage |
|---|---|---|
| `MAIN_FONT` | `Algerian` (overrides `fe/.env` `Algerian, fantasy`) | Site font (`mainFontEnv.js`). |
| `SPECIAL_LINK` / `SPECIAL_ID` / `SPECIAL_P` | set (password redacted) | Dev login prefill (`specialLoginEnv.js`). |
| `PRICE_PER_TOKEN` | `10` | Token pricing (`pricePerTokenEnv.js`). |
| `FE_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLE` | `false` (Mac `true`) | Browser API rate-limit master switch (`clientApiRateLimitEnv.js`). |
| `FE_RATE_CLIENT_API_*` | `100` / `60` s / `30` s / cooldown `true` / console `false` | Per-tab limit, window, cooldown, sub-switch, DevTools log. |
| `SELF_INTRO_VIDEO_MAX_LENGTH` | `60` (Mac `30`) | Self intro recorder max seconds (`selfIntroVideoMaxLengthEnv.js`). |
| `NOTES_DEFAULT_BUTTON_FONT_SIZE_REM` / `PHOTOALBUMS_DEFAULT_BUTTON_FONT_SIZE_REM` | `2` / `2` | Default vault button font size. |
| `ONENOTE_USB_UPGRADE` | `false` | `true` → mall TutaNotes / TutaPhotoAlbums tiles show upgrade popup (`onenoteUsbUpgradeEnv.js`). Also in `fe/.env` (`false`). |
| `*_VIDEO_TUTORIAL` (8 keys + alias `ACQUAINT_BUDDIES_VIDEO_TUTORIAL`) | `https://youtu.be/dMiwcH027fM` | Per-page **VIDEO TUTORIALS** header button (`pageVideoTutorialEnv.js`). |
| `SPEEDDATING` | `false` | `true` → Speed Dating sidebar item (`speedDatingEnv.js`). |
| `RAG_UI_ENABLED` | `true` | TutaNotes RAG assistant UI (`recordVaultRagUiEnv.js`). |
| `LEFT_SIDE` / `RIGHT_SIDE` | `TUTADRIVE` / `NONE` (Mac `TutaDrive` / `USB`) | `/myNote` panels (`rightSideEnv.js`; `RIGHT_SIDE` unset → `NOTES_LOCAL_USB`). |

Also exposed via prefix from `be.env` only when present in the Vite process env: `ALBUM_BINDER_WIDTH_PCT` (`albumBinderWidthEnv.js`, prod `15`), `SCAN_FOR_PHONE_UPLOAD_SEC` (`phoneUploadScanEnv.js`). Other FE-relevant BE config (`VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`, `NEW_ACCOUNT_SIGNUP`, `ONENOTE_USB_UPGRADE` runtime) comes through `/api` config endpoints, not the bundle.

## Theme and navigation

```bash
DEFAULT_THEME=Ocean Dark
DISABLE_NAVIGATION_COLLAPSE=false
MAIN_FONT=Algerian, fantasy
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `DEFAULT_THEME` | Initial theme for logged-out + new-account fallbacks (`defaultThemeEnv.js`). |
| `DISABLE_NAVIGATION_COLLAPSE` | `true` → sidebar stays expanded (`navigationCollapseEnv.js`). |
| `MAIN_FONT` | Fallback site font; **overridden by `~/.ssh/be/.env` `MAIN_FONT`** when set. Profile menu can override per browser / `user_customization.main_font`. |

## Build, API proxy, dev chrome

```bash
VITE_APP_VERSION=v5.1.0
GENERATE_SOURCEMAP=false
VITE_APP_BASE_NAME=/
API_PORT=40000
SHOW_ZOOM=true
VITE_SHOW_VIEWPORT_SIZE=true
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:40000
#VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://vsingles.club
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `VITE_APP_VERSION` | App version string in bundle. |
| `GENERATE_SOURCEMAP` | Production source maps. |
| `VITE_APP_BASE_NAME` | React Router basename. |
| `API_PORT` | Vite `/api` proxy target (`127.0.0.1:API_PORT`); `be/loadEnv.js` copies it to BE `PORT`. Must match `~/.ssh/be/.env`. |
| `SHOW_ZOOM` | Page zoom UI in `MainLayout` / `MinimalLayout`. |
| `VITE_SHOW_VIEWPORT_SIZE` | Lower-left viewport size overlay (`ViewportSizeReadout.jsx`). |
| `VITE_API_BASE_URL` | Optional full API origin overriding same-origin proxy (`apiBaseUrl.js`). Keep **unset** in production (FE + BE same origin). |

## Live face scan — manual video UI (Step 7B)

```bash
RECORD_VIDEO_TO_VW_RATIO=0.5
YELLOW_TEXT_BANNER_TO_VH_RATIO=0.25
```

`RECORD_VIDEO_TO_VW_RATIO` = record/replay frame width as fraction of popup content width; `YELLOW_TEXT_BANNER_TO_VH_RATIO` = instruction banner height as fraction of popup vh (width always 100%) (`liveFaceScanManualVideoEnv.js`).

