## Hover / sidebar zoom

```bash
HOVER_MAGNIFY_FACTOR=1.30
PRESS_HOLD_TO_ZOOM=false
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `HOVER_MAGNIFY_FACTOR` | Button label growth on hover/selected (`hoverMagnifyEnv.js`; `1.25` = +25%, button box unchanged). |
| `PRESS_HOLD_TO_ZOOM` | `true` → sidebar long-press keeps zoom; `false` → long-press suppresses zoom, quick tap still zooms (`pressHoldZoomEnv.js`). |

## My Picks layout / refresh

```bash
MY_PICKS_COLUMN_VW=21
MY_PICKS_COLUMN_VH=32
MY_PICKS_AVATAR_VW=9.2
MY_PICKS_AVATAR_VH=12
MY_PICKS_AVATAR_MOBILE_VW=28
MY_PICKS_REMOVE_X_SCALE=0.75
#VITE_MY_PICKS_LEGACY_REFRESH=true
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `MY_PICKS_COLUMN_*` | Left-column card size `min(Nvw, Nvh)` (`myPicksCardEnv.js`). |
| `MY_PICKS_AVATAR_*` | Avatar square on My Picks / photo gallery (mobile uses `_MOBILE_VW`). |
| `MY_PICKS_REMOVE_X_SCALE` | Remove-X size as fraction of half `DESKTOP_ICON_SIZE` (`0.75` = 25% smaller). |
| `VITE_MY_PICKS_LEGACY_REFRESH` | Unset/`false` = dedupe refresh on `/myPicks` visit (default); `true` = old extra refresh (`myPicksRefreshEnv.js`). |

## Auth dialogs / footer / legal pages

```bash
VERTICAL_SCROLLBAR=false
HORIZONTAL_SCROLLBAR=false
DIALOG_WIDTH_MOBILE=90
DIALOG_WIDTH_DESKTOP=50
DIALOG_MARGIN_TOP=2
DIALOG_MARGIN_BOT=4
FOOTER_HEIGHT=4
FOOTERPAGES_TOP_MARGIN=2
FOOTERPAGES_BOT_MARGIN=4
FOOTERPAGES_RIGHT_LEFT_MARGIN=2
```

| Variable | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `VERTICAL_SCROLLBAR` / `HORIZONTAL_SCROLLBAR` | Mobile auth dialog scrollbars only when `true` (`authDialogEnv.js`). |
| `DIALOG_WIDTH_MOBILE` / `_DESKTOP` | Standard auth dialog width % of vw (xs–sm / md+) (`standardAuthDialogEnv.js`). |
| `DIALOG_MARGIN_TOP` / `_BOT` | Top/bottom margin % of vh; dialog scrolls if content exceeds `100dvh` minus margins. |
| `FOOTER_HEIGHT` | Site-wide black fixed footer bar height % of vh (`authFooterEnv.js`). |
| `FOOTERPAGES_*` | About / Terms / Privacy scroll-column margins % vh/vw (`legalDialogEnv.js`) — not the footer bar. |

`DIALOG_ZOOM` / `DIALOG_HEIGHT_OFFSET` / `DIALOG_WIDGHT_OFFSET` live in `~/.ssh/be/.env` (both `100%` / `0%` / `0%`).

## Mall upgrade gate

```bash
ONENOTE_USB_UPGRADE=false
```

Fallback only — **`~/.ssh/be/.env` value wins** when set (see mirrored table). Runtime value is also served by `GET /api/publicConfig` → `onenoteUsbUpgrade` (`onenoteUsbUpgradeFe.js`).

## Dead keys in `fe/.env` (no reader in code)

| Key | Note |
|---|---|
| `FE_CHAT_SOCKET` | Reserved; nothing reads it. |
| `HOVER_ENLARGE_FACTOR` | Legacy name; runtime uses `HOVER_MAGNIFY_FACTOR`. |
| `TOOLTIP_DIALGO_WIDTH` | Empty, misspelled, no `TOOLTIP_` envPrefix, no reader. |
| `VSINGLES_SONG` | Exposed via `VSINGLES_` prefix but no code reads it. |

Safe to delete these lines (or wire them up) — changing them has no effect today.

## When changing these

1. Edit **`fe/.env`** for FE-only knobs; edit **`~/.ssh/be/.env`** for mirrored keys (it overrides `fe/.env`). Keep `API_PORT` identical in both.
2. Add any new client key with a prefix listed in `envPrefix` (or extend `envPrefix` / `BE_ENV_KEYS_FROM_HOME_FILE` in `fe/vite.config.mjs`).
3. Mac: restart **Vite** (`feall`). Ubuntu: re-run the PM2 FE build (`work2` / `febeprod`) so the bundle picks up new values.
4. Backend-only `~/.ssh/be/.env` changes: `pm2 restart onlinemallwebsite`.
